ANALYSIS SUMMARY
================================================================================

1. CARBONCAST CROSS-DOMAIN DEGRADATION:
   CarbonCast ZS / CarbonCast Supervised ratio:
   Mean: 1.28× (range: 0.87-2.39)
   CarbonCast loses 28% accuracy in cross-domain

2. TRANSCIF vs CARBONCAST ZERO-SHOT:
   TransCIF_ZS / CarbonCast_ZS ratio:
   Mean: 0.997
   TransCIF beats CarbonCast ZS in 5/9 regions
   TransCIF_ZS+ / CarbonCast_ZS ratio: Mean: 0.732
   TransCIF-ZS+ beats CarbonCast ZS in 8/9 regions

3. NORMALIZATION MISMATCH (root cause):
   Mean CIF range overlap (source vs target): 95.8%
   Regions with <50% overlap: 0/9
   This causes CarbonCast's denormalization to produce out-of-range predictions

4. KEY INSIGHT:
   CarbonCast fails because:
   a) Min-max normalization bakes in source domain statistics
   b) CNN-LSTM learns absolute CIF patterns (not relative/physics-based)
   c) No mechanism to adapt outputs to target domain emission factors
   TransCIF succeeds because:
   a) Predicts RENEWABLE SHARE (0-1, similar across all regions)
   b) Physics layer converts to CIF using target's config (ef_r, ef_nr)
   c) Config-weighted sampling focuses on relevant source regions

